From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Meumertzheim <fabian@meumertzhe.im>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crt: Fix #ifndef F_X86_NATIVE in func.def.in

The guard checked `F_X86_NATIVE(x)` instead of the macro name, which is
diagnosed as "extra tokens at end of #ifndef directive" (-Wextra-tokens)
when preprocessing .def.in files without -Wp,-w.

Signed-off-by: Fabian Meumertzheim <fabian@meumertzhe.im>
---
 mingw-w64-crt/def-include/func.def.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mingw-w64-crt/def-include/func.def.in b/mingw-w64-crt/def-include/func.def.in
index 7663e01b..9a7960ec 100644
--- a/mingw-w64-crt/def-include/func.def.in
+++ b/mingw-w64-crt/def-include/func.def.in
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 #ifndef F_X86_ANY
 #define F_X86_ANY(x)
 #endif
-#ifndef F_X86_NATIVE(x)
+#ifndef F_X86_NATIVE
 #define F_X86_NATIVE(x)
 #endif
 #ifndef F_I386
